...me?

477
01:10:47,998 --> 01:10:51,198
Yes, I was talking to you.
You was really great back there.

478
01:10:51,398 --> 01:10:54,598
Those guards, they thought they was
all that. You showed up, and bam!

479
01:10:54,798 --> 01:10:57,038
Tripping over themselves
like babes in the woods.

480
01:10:57,238 --> 01:10:59,238
That really made me
feel good to see that.

481
01:10:59,438 --> 01:11:01,638
That's great. Really.
Man, it's good to be free.

482
01:11:02,078 --> 01:11:05,919
Now, why don't you go celebrate
your freedom with your own friends?

483
01:11:06,079 --> 01:11:07,599
Hm?

484
01:11:07,759 --> 01:11:09,199
But, uh...

485
01:11:09,439 --> 01:11:10,999
...I don't have any friends.

486
01:11:11,159 --> 01:11:13,639
And I'm not going out there by myself.

487
01:11:13,799 --> 01:11:16,439
Wait a minute. I got a great idea.
I'll stick with you!

488
01:11:16,599 --> 01:11:18,359
<i>DONKEY:
You a mean, green fighting machine.</i>

489
01:11:18,559 --> 01:11:21,639
<i>Together we'll scare the spit
out of anybody that crosses us.</i>

490
01:11:24,879 --> 01:11:26,159
<i>I like Shrek.</i>

491
01:11:26,319 --> 01:11:28,759
<i>DONKEY: That was really scary.
If you don't mind me saying...</i>

492
01:11:28,919 --> 01:11:31,639
<i>...if that don't work, your breath
will get the job done...</i>

493
01:11:31,839 --> 01:11:35,760
<i>...because you definitely need some
tic tacs, because your breath stinks!</i>

494
01:11:36,360 --> 01:11:40,400
<i>Man, you almost burned the hair
out of my nose. Just like the time....</i>

495
01:11:42,880 --> 01:11:45,480
You're not so good with people anymore,
are you?

496
01:11:50,960 --> 01:11:53,480
Thank you for my leg.

497
01:11:56,000 --> 01:11:57,760
Okay.

498
01:12:00,841 --> 01:12:02,361
Where have you been?

499
01:12:02,601 --> 01:12:06,161
I was on a Red Cross evacuation ship
out of Säo Paulo.

500
01:12:06,321 --> 01:12:09,441
Those boats
weren't meant to be permanent.

501
01:12:09,601 --> 01:12:11,161
No, they weren't.

502
01:12:11,321 --> 01:12:14,321
When the Navy fell apart,
we started docking to take on supplies.

503
01:12:14,521 --> 01:12:18,281
Someone picked it up on shore.
Five of us were immune.

504
01:12:18,441 --> 01:12:20,081
You said five?

505
01:12:20,761 --> 01:12:23,161
The Darkseekers got them.

506
01:12:25,521 --> 01:12:28,162
You are the Robert Neville, aren't you?

507
01:12:37,002 --> 01:12:38,362
It's too late today.

508
01:12:38,522 --> 01:12:41,642
lf we leave tomorrow at dawn, we can
make it to Vermont in a straight shot.

509
01:12:41,842 --> 01:12:44,282
-So if you had--
-I'm not leaving.

510
01:12:45,162 --> 01:12:47,482
This is ground zero.

511
01:12:48,922 --> 01:12:51,082
This is my site.

512
01:12:52,762 --> 01:12:55,242
I'm not gonna let this happen.

513
01:12:57,403 --> 01:12:59,723
I can still fix this.

514
01:13:04,523 --> 01:13:06,483
What happened to your leg?

515
01:13:09,003 --> 01:13:13,083
That's my snare.
These are my materials.

516
01:13:13,283 --> 01:13:16,283
The infected didn't do this. They can't.

517
01:13:16,843 --> 01:13:20,123
-How do you know?
-They have no higher brain function.

518
01:13:20,323 --> 01:13:25,564
They don't plan or hate.
They don't love. They can't.

519
01:13:30,204 --> 01:13:31,764
ANNA:
Could they be evolving?

520
01:13:38,204 --> 01:13:40,044
ANNA:
Ethan.

521
01:13:43,684 --> 01:13:45,764
Hey, Ethan.

522
01:13:54,165 --> 01:13:55,285
It's cold.

523
01:14:04,085 --> 01:14:05,125
We gotta go.

524
01:14:07,685 --> 01:14:09,805
ROBERT: I've been cooking the compounds.
ANNA: What?

525
01:14:10,005 --> 01:14:12,405
ROBERT:
Ice. I need ice.

526
01:14:20,886 --> 01:14:25,566
ROBERT: Whoa. You scared me.
-Sorry.

527
01:14:25,726 --> 01:14:27,086
I called down twice.

528
01:14:27,246 --> 01:14:29,886
Oh. Oh, thank you.

529
01:14:34,566 --> 01:14:38,166
It's heavily sedated.
Don't worry, it's safe.

530
01:14:38,366 --> 01:14:41,086
I've never seen one so still.

531
01:14:41,686 --> 01:14:44,366
They're always biting.

532
01:14:48,407 --> 01:14:50,727
You think that can cure her?

533
01:14:50,887 --> 01:14:53,847
Um.... No, this will
almost certainly kill it...

534
01:14:54,007 --> 01:14:57,247
...but it's possible by drastically reducing
the body temperature...

535
01:14:57,407 --> 01:15:00,407
...I can increase the compound's
effectiveness.

536
01:15:11,687 --> 01:15:13,968
Did all of them die?

537
01:15:14,208 --> 01:15:15,768
Yes.

538
01:15:18,848 --> 01:15:20,848
ANNA:
My God.

539
01:15:21,688 --> 01:15:25,448
God didn't do this, Anna, we did.

540
01:15:30,768 --> 01:15:33,088
Where can Ethan sleep?

541
01:15:51,809 --> 01:15:53,649
He's heavy.

542
01:16:00,169 --> 01:16:01,969
Can you get that?

543
01:16:33,770 --> 01:16:36,051
ANNA:
She's beautiful.

544
01:16:36,531 --> 01:16:38,451
What's her name?

545
01:16:40,131 --> 01:16:42,051
Marley.

546
01:16:43,331 --> 01:16:46,891
-Her name was Marley.
-It's a beautiful name.

547
01:16:48,771 --> 01:16:52,811
Yeah. We named her after Bob Marley.

548
01:16:53,011 --> 01:16:56,331
-Who?
-Uh, the singer.

549
01:16:57,371 --> 01:16:59,091
Damian?

550
01:17:00,371 --> 01:17:02,371
Uh, his father.

551
01:17:05,652 --> 01:17:07,932
His father.

552
01:17:09,012 --> 01:17:10,132
Nope.

553
01:17:10,292 --> 01:17:12,412
I shot the sheriff

554
01:17:15,732 --> 01:17:18,692
<i>But I didn't shoot the deputy</i>

555
01:17:26,212 --> 01:17:31,213
-Oh, that is unacceptable.
-What?

556
01:17:35,853 --> 01:17:38,373
Best album ever made.

557
01:17:42,533 --> 01:17:45,333
[BOB MARLEY'S ''STlR lT UP''
PLAYS ON STEREO]

558
01:17:47,733 --> 01:17:50,773
-You don't recognize that?
-Mm-mm.

559
01:17:52,093 --> 01:17:53,333
Wow.

560
01:17:55,493 --> 01:18:01,054
He had this idea,
it was kind of a virologist's idea.

561
01:18:01,214 --> 01:18:05,854
He believed that you could cure
racism and hate. Literally cure it...

562
01:18:06,054 --> 01:18:12,174
...by injecting music and love
into people's lives.

563
01:18:13,014 --> 01:18:16,894
One day, he was scheduled
to perform at a peace rally.

564
01:18:17,054 --> 01:18:21,014
Gunmen came to his house
and shot him down.

565
01:18:22,854 --> 01:18:24,174
Two days later...

566
01:18:24,814 --> 01:18:28,455
...he walked out on that stage and sang.

567
01:18:30,255 --> 01:18:32,655
Somebody asked him why.

568
01:18:34,455 --> 01:18:36,935
He said, ''The people...

569
01:18:37,095 --> 01:18:42,175
...who are trying to make this world worse
are not taking a day off.

570
01:18:43,335 --> 01:18:45,335
How can I?''

571
01:18:48,415 --> 01:18:51,255
Light up the darkness.

572
01:19:17,256 --> 01:19:19,496
Come with us, Neville.

573
01:19:20,096 --> 01:19:22,097
To the colony.

574
01:19:25,817 --> 01:19:28,257
There's no colony, Anna.

575
01:19:32,537 --> 01:19:34,097
Everything just fell apart.

576
01:19:34,257 --> 01:19:37,937
-There was no evacuation plan--
-You're wrong. There is a colony.

577
01:19:38,537 --> 01:19:40,537
I know, okay?

578
01:19:42,017 --> 01:19:43,217
How do you know, Anna?

579
01:19:49,738 --> 01:19:50,818
I just know.

580
01:19:53,098 --> 01:19:57,218
How? I said, how do you know?
How could you know?

581
01:19:58,898 --> 01:20:00,258
God told me.

582
01:20:00,738 --> 01:20:02,738
He has a plan.

583
01:20:04,498 --> 01:20:07,098
-God told you?
-Yes.

584
01:20:07,258 --> 01:20:09,978
-The God?
-Yes.

585
01:20:11,578 --> 01:20:13,978
-I know how this sounds.
-It sounds crazy.

586
01:20:14,178 --> 01:20:17,979
But something told me
to turn on the radio.

587
01:20:18,139 --> 01:20:19,779
Something told me to come here.

588
01:20:19,939 --> 01:20:22,739
My voice on the radio
told you to come here, Anna.

589
01:20:22,899 --> 01:20:24,939
You were trying to kill yourself
last night?

590
01:20:25,099 --> 01:20:26,099
Anna.

591
01:20:26,259 --> 01:20:29,459
I got here just in time to save your life.
That's a coincidence?

592
01:20:29,619 --> 01:20:33,259
<i>-Just stop it. Stop it. Stop.
-He must have sent me here for a reason.</i>

593
01:20:34,419 --> 01:20:37,459
Neville, the world is quieter now.

594
01:20:37,619 --> 01:20:39,699
You just have to listen.

595
01:20:39,859 --> 01:20:42,019
lf we listen...

596
01:20:42,699 --> 01:20:44,660
...we can hear God's plan.

597
01:20:44,860 --> 01:20:46,900
-God's plan?
-Yeah.

598
01:20:47,060 --> 01:20:49,620
All right. Let me tell you
about your God's plan.

599
01:20:49,820 --> 01:20:52,700
There were 6 billion people on Earth
when the infection hit.

600
01:20:52,860 --> 01:20:57,460
KV had a 90 percent kill rate.
That's 5.4 billion...

601
01:20:57,660 --> 01:21:00,100
...people dead.

602
01:21:00,260 --> 01:21:03,100
Crashed and bled out, dead.

603
01:21:03,300 --> 01:21:05,140
Less than 1 percent immunity.

604
01:21:05,300 --> 01:21:09,100
That left 1 2 million healthy people
like you, me and Ethan.

605
01:21:09,300 --> 01:21:13,421
The other 588 million...

606
01:21:13,581 --> 01:21:15,581
...turned into your Darkseekers.

607
01:21:15,781 --> 01:21:17,461
And then they got hungry.

608
01:21:17,621 --> 01:21:22,021
And they killed and fed on everybody.

609
01:21:23,221 --> 01:21:25,301
Everybody!

610
01:21:26,021 --> 01:21:30,981
Every single person
that you or I has ever known...

611
01:21:31,141 --> 01:21:33,061
...is dead!

612
01:21:35,421 --> 01:21:37,301
Dead!

613
01:21:38,662 --> 01:21:41,382
There is no God. There is no God.

614
01:21:46,702 --> 01:21:48,542
What is that?

615
01:21:51,862 --> 01:21:55,182
Was it still dark when you
brought us home last night?

616
01:21:55,382 --> 01:21:58,462
You were bleeding.
There was light on the horizon.

617
01:22:00,062 --> 01:22:02,782
Turn the light off. Turn it off.

618
01:22:10,063 --> 01:22:11,503
They followed us home.

619
01:22:11,663 --> 01:22:13,303
Ethan.

620
01:22:59,504 --> 01:23:01,145
Shit.

621
01:23:13,905 --> 01:23:15,505
Anna.

622
01:23:17,065 --> 01:23:18,865
Anna.

623
01:23:23,625 --> 01:23:25,265
Anna!

624
01:23:36,866 --> 01:23:38,826
Anna!

625
01:23:42,226 --> 01:23:43,826
Anna!

626
01:25:30,263 --> 01:25:31,863
Anna?

627
01:25:35,863 --> 01:25:37,583
Anna.

628
01:26:35,462 --> 01:26:37,662
Come on. Come on.

629
01:26:38,702 --> 01:26:40,662
-Are you okay? You all right?
ANNA: Yeah.

630
01:26:40,822 --> 01:26:42,342
Are you all right?

631
01:26:42,982 --> 01:26:44,381
-You okay?
-Oh, my God. You're bleeding.

632
01:26:58,781 --> 01:27:01,381
Go to the lab. Downstairs, go!

633
01:27:01,661 --> 01:27:04,421
Get to the lab! To the lab!

634
01:27:13,781 --> 01:27:14,821
Get behind the Plexi.

635
01:27:15,661 --> 01:27:17,301
Oh, my God. Come on.

636
01:27:29,900 --> 01:27:31,660
Come on, it's okay. It's okay.

637
01:27:33,460 --> 01:27:35,220
Oh, my God.

638
01:27:47,740 --> 01:27:49,700
It's working.

639
01:27:54,060 --> 01:27:55,420
Neville...

640
01:27:56,740 --> 01:27:58,540
...it's working.

641
01:28:03,820 --> 01:28:05,619
No! Stop! Stop!

642
01:28:06,939 --> 01:28:09,219
Look, look, look, I can save you.

643
01:28:09,419 --> 01:28:12,859
I can sa-- I can help you.
You are sick and I can help you.

644
01:28:15,979 --> 01:28:17,939
I can-- I can fix this!

645
01:28:18,099 --> 01:28:19,659
I can save everybody!

646
01:28:19,819 --> 01:28:23,059
I can fix everything! It's working.
It's working!

647
01:28:26,299 --> 01:28:27,739
Stop! Stop!

648
01:28:33,859 --> 01:28:37,299
Let me save you! Let me save you!

649
01:28:37,459 --> 01:28:38,459
No, no!

650
01:28:49,298 --> 01:28:50,618
No, no!

651
01:29:20,058 --> 01:29:22,818
<i>MARLEY:
Daddy, look, it's a butterfly.</i>

652
01:30:01,257 --> 01:30:02,817
Robert.

653
01:30:03,937 --> 01:30:05,937
What are you doing?

654
01:30:33,856 --> 01:30:35,296
Open the door, please.

655
01:30:37,616 --> 01:30:38,776
What are you doing?

656
01:30:40,696 --> 01:30:42,456
I'm listening.

657
01:31:06,055 --> 01:31:08,095
ANNA:
Shh, shh, shh....

658
01:31:08,655 --> 01:31:10,135
Don't look.

659
01:31:41,934 --> 01:31:43,694
I need to get a syringe.

660
01:33:18,412 --> 01:33:19,652
I'm sorry.

661
01:34:23,130 --> 01:34:25,010
ANNA:
Shh, shh, shh....

662
01:34:38,548 --> 01:34:39,883
WARNING
RESTRICTED AREA

663
01:34:39,890 --> 01:34:41,650
My name is Anna Montez.

664
01:34:43,170 --> 01:34:45,170
<i>There are other survivors.</i>

665
01:34:47,250 --> 01:34:51,569
<i>I am traveling with Dr. Robert Neville
and a boy named Ethan.</i>

666
01:34:51,729 --> 01:34:56,649
<i>We're heading north on Route 17
to Bethel, Vermont.</i>

667
01:34:56,809 --> 01:35:01,849
<i>Keep your radio on.
Listen for our broadcasts.</i>

668
01:35:02,329 --> 01:35:04,889
<i>You are not alone.</i>

669
01:35:05,729 --> 01:35:08,129
<i>There is hope.</i>

670
01:35:09,329 --> 01:35:11,489
<i>Keep listening.</i>

671
01:35:12,809 --> 01:35:14,649
<i>You are not alone.</i>

672
01:36:27,865 --> 01:36:32,036
I AM LEGEND

